 🚨 Explosive new reporting led by The New York Times' Jonathan Swan and Maggie Haberman reveals a Chinese executive with close ties to Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang passed intel directly to Beijing. President Trump was briefed on the breach and took no action. The Times says the executive, Alice Huang, remains employed by her company and is under surveillance. ( Gift link .)

 ⚖️ Weil, Gotshal &amp; Manges, a white-shoe Wall Street law firm that led some of the biggest bankruptcies in history, plans to dissolve after the defection of key partners and a failed merger deal. Read on . 

 
 
