 4. 🗳️ Early voting surge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Axios research. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios More than 39 million Americans have cast early votes so far — with unusually strong turnout among Black, Hispanic and unaffiliated voters in several states, Axios' Josephine Walker writes. 

 Overall turnout could rival the 2018 "blue wave," which saw the highest participation rate since 1914, University of Florida political scientist Michael McDonald says. Keep reading . 

 
 
