 7. 🚀 Cape Canaveral&#x27;s new &quot;boom cycle&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A Falcon 9 rocket mission from Space Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral earlier this month. Photo: Gwendolyn Kurzen/Defense Department Thomas Novelly, author of Axios Future of Defense's space edition, writes: 

 Rocket launches from Florida's Cape Canaveral are now outpacing those of the Cold War-era space race that first made the launch site famous.

 Why it matters: U.S. leaders are rushing to grow the number of rocket providers at America's busiest spaceport amid a space and arms race with China. 🛰️ Behind the scenes: Cape Canaveral is busy expanding to meet President Trump's mandate for the U.S. to support 1,000 annual launches by 2030.

 SpaceX is expanding its footprint on the Cape for its Starship super heavy-lift launchpads. NASA is preparing for next year's Artemis III test missions and the Artemis IV voyage that aims to return astronauts to the moon by 2028. Blue Origin is rapidly rebuilding its launch complex after its New Glenn rocket exploded in May. Keep reading . 

 
 
