 8. ⚾ 1 fun thing: Brew Crew champs 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Milwaukee Brewers celebrate after winning the World Series over the Tampa Bay Rays last night at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Fla. Photo: Al Bello/Getty Images The small-ball Milwaukee Brewers — playing in the smallest market in the majors — are World Series champions for the first time in franchise history.

 The Brewers dominated 4-1 in Game 5 last night to complete a gentleman's sweep of the Tampa Bay Rays and set off a long-awaited celebration among thousands of Brewers fans at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Fla. Brewers star Jacob "Miz" Misiorowski pitches last night. Photo: Carmen Mandato/Getty Images 🔮 What's next: This might have been the last Major League Baseball game for an extended period.

 A lockout is likely to start Dec. 2 and could threaten the 2027 season. By the numbers ... More on the game . 

 
 
